From 9386d5ed59da439acc534fa4c138fe709e53f031 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:58:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] round C1.5: bridge starts a business session for every
 sign-in in a tab

Round C1.4 R3: after one account signed out and an existing account signed
in on the same page, the second account had no business token until the
page was reloaded (DB: no new business_tokens row until the reload).

Cause: GoldenSessionBridge guarded the start with a boolean ref that was
set on the first sign-in and never cleared. Clerk's signOut({redirectUrl})
navigates inside the app, so the root-layout component is not remounted;
the ref stayed true and the next sign-in skipped startBusinessSession.

Fix:
- the guard is keyed by Clerk userId (startedFor), and cleared on every
  signed-out render, so any later sign-in - same user or another - starts;
- the effect also depends on userId;
- a direct user switch with no signed-out render in between (multi-session)
  clears the stored marker/credential first, so the previous user's token
  is never resumed for the new user.

Unchanged: read-before-mint order, revoke-on-signed-out path, signOut
handle and events, no new state. File is in Aika's area; for her review.

Note (not changed here): /golden/session/verify resolves a business token
without checking it belongs to the current Clerk user; the bridge-side
switch guard covers the browser path, the server-side binding is a
separate backend decision.

Test: scripts/test-golden-bridge-user-switch.cjs (5) renders the real
component with hook doubles; fails against the previous bridge (second
sign-in never starts). c2-clerk golden-session 23/23, sign-out 7/7,
candidate-shape 8/8 locally.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0187FcquTLWgvavMDgSvEHQp
